<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/inventions?focus=brahmi-script">Inventions &amp; Discoveries</a> · Writing and counting</p><h1 class="enc-title">Brahmi script</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">3rd century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century-bce">3rd century BCE</a> · Also known as Brāhmī</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Brahmi is a writing system of ancient <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> that appeared as a fully developed script in the 3rd century BCE; its earliest securely dated inscriptions are the rock-cut edicts of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashoka">Ashoka</a>, from 250–232 BCE. It is an abugida, marking vowels with signs attached to consonants. Its origin is much debated: most scholars derive it from, or see the influence of, a Semitic script such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aramaic">Aramaic</a>. Deciphered by James Prinsep in the 1830s, it is the ancestor of the Brahmic scripts still used across South and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/southeast-asia">Southeast Asia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/brahmi-script.jpg" alt="Brahmi script" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Brahmi_pillar_inscription_in_Sarnath.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="inv-entry"><h2 class="enc-section-title">On the inventions tree</h2><dl class="inv-entry-facts"><div><dt>First known</dt><dd>3rd century BCE</dd></div><div><dt>Where</dt><dd>India</dd></div><div><dt>Credited to</dt><dd><a href="/empire/maurya-empire">Maurya Empire</a></dd></div></dl><p class="inv-entry-note"><span class="inv-k">Note</span>Most scholars derive it from a Semitic script, usually Aramaic; earlier inscribed potsherds from Sri Lanka and Tamil Nadu are disputed.</p><div class="inv-entry-rel"><span class="inv-k">Built on</span><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/phoenician-alphabet">Phoenician alphabet<span>c. 1050 BCE</span></a></div><div class="inv-entry-rel"><span class="inv-k">Led to</span><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/hindu-arabic-numeral-system">Hindu–Arabic numerals<span>1st–4th century CE</span></a></div><p class="enc-article-foot"><a class="enc-random-link" href="/inventions?focus=brahmi-script">See it on the inventions tree &rarr;</a></p></section>
